# ADR-0002 ballots — MTG-2026-11-14-invoice-storage

Mode: subagent debate (Agent Teams unavailable in this cloud session). No Secretary, no hook event log. Capture: **NOT VERIFIED**.
Voters (each run read-only; model override: haiku, chosen by the lead to fit the $2 session budget): data-platform-engineer, domain-architect, security-reviewer, devil-advocate.
Round 1 used an identical brief with no peer output. Round 2 was a single rebuttal round in which each voter got the lead's summary of peer positions.

## Criteria and weights (lead-set, adapted from the skill's default)
Durability 25%, security/tenant isolation 20%, delivery complexity 20% (5 = simplest), operating cost 15% (5 = cheapest), scaling/extensibility 10%, testability 10%. The UX/product-fit weights were dropped because this is a backend storage choice with no UI surface.

## Round 1 matrix rows (verbatim scores, A / B / C)

| Voter | Durability | Security | Delivery | Cost | Scaling | Testability | Total A | Total B | Total C |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| data-platform-engineer | 1/4/5 | 2/3/4 | 5/4/2 | 5/4/2 | 1/3/5 | 3/4/3 | 2.80 | 3.70 | 3.55 |
| domain-architect | 1/4/5 | 2/3/4 | 5/4/2 | 5/4/2 | 1/2/4 | 5/4/3 | 3.00 | 3.60 | 3.45 |
| security-reviewer | 1/4/5 | 2/3/4 | 5/4/2 | 5/4/2 | 1/2/5 | 5/4/3 | 3.00 | 3.60 | 3.55 |
| devil-advocate | 1/4/5 | 2/3/4 | 5/4/2 | 5/4/2 | 1/2/5 | 5/4/3 | 3.00 | 3.60 | 3.55 |

## Round 1 FINAL_BALLOTs (verbatim)
- `FINAL_BALLOT: voter=database-engineer; choice=B; state=EXPERIMENT; conditions=persistent disk confirmed for single instance; engines or driver approval given; orgId-scoped schema and tests; switch to C if hosting or scale changes` (The voter label was wrong; the voter corrected it in round 2.)
- `FINAL_BALLOT: voter=architect; choice=B; state=EXPERIMENT; conditions=hosting confirms a persistent volume; a POST/write path is added and tested; orgId filter and tenant isolation tests pass; owner confirms the decision; switch to C if any "what would change my mind" trigger occurs.`
- `FINAL_BALLOT: voter=security-reviewer; choice=B; state=EXPERIMENT; conditions=persistent volume confirmed by hosting decision; orgId derived from authenticated identity (server.js:9 fixed) before release; tenant-scoped queries with tests; revisit to C on multi-instance or load evidence`
- `FINAL_BALLOT: voter=devil-advocate; choice=B; state=EXPERIMENT; conditions=hosting confirmed with persistent disk and backups; repository port with contract tests runnable on SQLite and later Postgres; "lost on restart" reproduced first; x-org-id auth gap escalated to owner before tenant data is stored; revisit if a multi-instance or load requirement appears`

## Round 2 (rebuttal) score changes, as stated by each voter
- data-platform-engineer: base scores unchanged. Their note that "delivery complexity for B rises by one point if the write path must be built first" is ambiguous (direction unclear, C not addressed), so it is **not applied**. No-disk sensitivity: B 2.95.
